---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
---
<Base
  title="mbem — Examples"
  description="Move three slices through a stored mollified BEM solution: four material and surface states, three fields, and the near-boundary quality threshold."
  current="examples"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    <h1>Examples<span class="sub">a stored solve, explored</span></h1>
    <p>
      Nothing is computed here. The solve &mdash; 24,348 unknowns, a dense LU
      reference and a block-compressed operator agreeing to ~2&times;10<sup>&minus;6</sup>
      &mdash; ran in Python; this page moves three slices through its stored
      readout.
    </p>
    <p>
      Four <b>states</b> share one geometry: the surface is flat or carries the
      hill, and the inclusion is soft or identical to its host. Differencing them
      isolates each effect, which is only well defined because every state was
      sampled on the same grid.
    </p>
    <div class="note">
      The <b>quality</b> slider is the one to play with. It hides cells closer
      than <i>d</i>/<i>h</i> to a solved boundary. The topography effect reads
      1287&nbsp;mm at a point lying on the free surface and 96&nbsp;mm at
      <i>d</i>/<i>h</i>&nbsp;&gt;&nbsp;0.5 &mdash; a factor of 33 that is
      discretization, not physics.
    </div>
    <p class="contact">
      Fields are shown on a <b>log</b> colour scale: they span about five
      decades, and a linear scale shows only the fault.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <div id="viewer" class="viewer">
    <div class="panel">
      <label><span>State</span><span data-ctl="state"></span></label>
      <label><span>Field</span><span data-ctl="field"></span></label>
      <label><span>Colours</span><span data-ctl="map"></span></label>
      <label><span>Quality</span><span data-ctl="threshold" class="rng"></span></label>
    </div>
    <div data-canvas class="canvas"></div>
    <div data-bar class="bar"></div>
    <div class="panel slices">
      <label><span>x slice</span><span data-ctl="slice-x" class="rng"></span></label>
      <label><span>y slice</span><span data-ctl="slice-y" class="rng"></span></label>
      <label><span>z slice</span><span data-ctl="slice-z" class="rng"></span></label>
    </div>
    <p data-status class="status">loading&hellip;</p>
  </div>

  <p class="cap">
    Pink outlines the fault, blue the inclusion, grey the box and the free
    surface. Stress is the <b>elastic</b> part: the eigenstress
    <i>C</i>:&epsilon;* that every mollified jump carries has been subtracted, which
    is what makes an on-fault value mean anything. See
    <a href={`${base}concepts/`}>Concepts</a>.
  </p>

  <style is:global>
    #viewer { margin-bottom: 18px; }
    #viewer .canvas { width: 100%; min-height: 440px; cursor: grab; background: #fff; }
    #viewer .canvas:active { cursor: grabbing; }
    #viewer .canvas canvas { display: block; }
    #viewer .panel {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 18px; align-items: center;
      margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 13px;
    }
    #viewer .panel label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
    #viewer .panel label > span:first-child { color: var(--fg-dim); }
    #viewer .panel select { font: inherit; font-size: 13px; padding: 2px 4px; }
    #viewer .panel .rng { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
    #viewer .panel input[type="range"] { width: 120px; }
    #viewer .panel .val { color: var(--fg-dim); min-width: 84px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    #viewer .slices { margin-top: 10px; }
    #viewer .bar { margin-top: 8px; }
    #viewer .bar .strip { height: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    #viewer .bar .ends {
      display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--fg-dim); margin-top: 3px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    #viewer .bar .ends .mid { color: var(--fg-faint); }
    #viewer .status { font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg-dim); margin-top: 8px; }
    .cap { font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg-dim); }
    .cap b { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  </style>
  <script>
    import { startViewer } from "../viz/controls";
    startViewer(document.getElementById("viewer")!, import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
  </script>
</Base>
